./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:345:1. **Completeness licence.** Affine singularity completeness is closed by the delta budget (`p_a = g_{\mathrm{geom}} + \Delta_{\mathrm{aff}} + \delta_\infty`) together with an exact node/fibre check on the displayed curve, not by a derivative-only argument.
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:346:2. **Newton face QUARANTINED at row level.** Infinity Puiseux is computed on the displayed curve only. Extra AG-S lower terms may change weights; no universal raw `(Y,Z)` face is claimed for every reduced `(9,6,4)` equation.
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:349:Protocol: (i) reduced-sequence verification; (ii) AG-S associated curve plus a polynomial (normalisation `A^1`) member if the associated curve is not charged; (iii) infinity analysis of the displayed curve; (iv) licensing reads of BL 2014, BHL 2017, BLZ 2024 Thm 6.4, FLMN 2006 — evaluate if a variant applies; (v) verdict `KILLED` / `PASS_NECESSARY_ONLY` / `OPEN`.
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:353:## 2. Reduced-sequence verification for (9,6,4)
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:355:Assi–García-Sánchez, arXiv:1407.0490v1, definition before Proposition 13 and Proposition 2. Write `r=(r_0,r_1,r_2)=(9,6,4)`.
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:375:The Abhyankar semigroup is `Γ=⟨9,6,4⟩=⟨4,6,9⟩`, the *same numerical semigroup* as the twin row `(6,4,9)`. Gaps `{1,2,3,5,7,11}`, six gaps, conductor 12. The two census survivors are the two reduced δ-sequences of this semigroup; AG-S Theorem 14 therefore forbids relating them by an automorphism of `K[x,y]`.
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:389:## 3. AG-S associated curve, parametrization, and complete singularity record
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:413:The associated curve is not a census representative. A proper polynomial parametrisation of degrees `(9,6)` with `deg(y^3-x^2)=4` realises the reduced sequence on a rational one-place curve. In the even/odd family
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:435:`r_0=deg_t x=9`, `r_1=deg_t y=6`, `r_2=deg_t(y^3-x^2)=4`, so the δ-sequence is `(9,6,4)`. The value semigroup contains `⟨4,6,9⟩`; with this sequence of length 3 it equals `⟨4,6,9⟩`, genus 6, therefore `Δ_{\mathrm{aff}}=6`.
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:450:Remaining delta 2 cannot be a three-branch germ (minimum delta 3 for three smooth branches). It cannot be unibranch (the parametrisation is an immersion). It is therefore a two-smooth-branch germ, hence of type `A_{2n-1}` with link `T(2,2n)`: either two further nodes, or one `A_3` (`n=2`). Both lie in BLZ 2024 Theorem 6.4. The split is not needed for licensing.
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:454:  four ordinary nodes (t ↔ -t on x=0), plus remaining δ=2 of type T(2,2n)
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:459:This representative is not row-exhaustion and is not `FULL_ACTUAL_EXIT`. Other AG-S moduli may change the affine partition. It is the first explicit charged curve of the row `(9,6,4)`.
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:472:so `v(Y)=3` and `v(Z)=9\in⟨3⟩`. Homogenising a degree-9 equation, `p_a=28`; with `g_{\mathrm{geom}}=0` and `Δ_{\mathrm{aff}}=6` one has `δ_∞=22`. A unibranch germ with `v(Y)=3` and delta 22 has characteristic valuation `v(Z-Y^3)=23` and local semigroup `S_∞=⟨3,23⟩`: the coprime formula `(3-1)(23-1)/2=22` matches the budget, and the expansion already matches `Z` against `Y^3` through order `s^{17}`, consistent with a later first difference at order 23. Link `T(3,23)`. Conductor of `⟨3,23⟩` is `3\cdot 23-3-23=43`.
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:478:  semigroup        = ⟨3,23⟩
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:488:The associated (genus-3) curve of §3.1 has the *same* local infinity semigroup `⟨3,23⟩` on its own Newton face `(Y^3-Z)^3=Y^2 Z^7`; that computation is not transported to other moduli. Extra AG-S terms of `fint<12` can change weights on other members of the family (the quarantine). The charged curve’s infinity is read from its parametrisation and the delta budget, not from that face.
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:490:## 5. Licensing reads against BL / BHL / BLZ / FLMN
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:494:**BL 2014, Theorems 5.4 / 6.5.** Rational cuspidal curves: every singularity unibranch, geometric genus 0. The charged curve has four ordinary nodes. Hypothesis fails. The associated curve of §3.1 fails both rationality and the unibranch condition (`A_5`).
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:500:**BLZ 2024, Theorem 6.4** (the applicable variant). Reduced curve of degree `d` and genus `g`, cuspidal points with counting functions `R_i`, and apart from those only singularities whose links are `T(2,2n)`, with `η_+=\sum m_n`, `κ_+=\sum n m_n`. Then for `k=1,\ldots,d-2`, writing `R` for the infimal convolution of the `R_i` and `RHS=(k+1)(k+2)/2`,
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:507:The charged curve has `d=9`, `g=0`, one cusp `S_∞=⟨3,23⟩`, and affine singularities only of type `T(2,2n)`. Two licensed remaining-delta splits:
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:511:B:  four nodes + A_3   m_1=4, m_2=1    η_+=5, κ_+=6,  κ_+-η_+=1
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:526:Second inequality is independent of the `A`/`B` split (`κ_+` agrees). All fourteen comparisons hold; `k=6,7` saturate the second inequality. **No KILL.** The associated genus-3 curve of §3.1 is likewise in BLZ scope (`g=3`, one `T(2,6)` so `η_+=1`, `κ_+=3`) and exists, so its inequalities cannot fail; it is not a charged representative.
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:528:BL 2014 Theorem 6.5 is not evaluated on the candidate (nodes present). Evaluating a fictional unibranch affine semigroup would fill a missing dictionary by analogy, which the protocol forbids.
./xmodel/hf-twin-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:530:## 6. Twin comparison: (9,6,4) versus (6,4,9)
