./xmodel/hf-twin-964-grok46-20260831.md:148:Remaining delta 2 cannot be a three-branch germ (minimum delta 3 for three smooth branches). It cannot be unibranch (the parametrisation is an immersion). It is therefore a two-smooth-branch germ, hence of type `A_{2n-1}` with link `T(2,2n)`: either two further nodes, or one `A_3` (`n=2`). Both lie in BLZ 2024 Theorem 6.4. The split is not needed for licensing.
