./xmodel/m-inf-hostile-review-sol56-20260831.log:314:    10	**Convention lock (preview).** Characteristic data, semigroup generators, and the last exponent `beta_h` are typed in §1; every later formula uses that lock.
./xmodel/m-inf-hostile-review-sol56-20260831.log:342:    38	The original Abhyankar–Moh 1975 PDF (Crelle 276, 148–166) was **not obtained** from an official free source (De Gruyter paywall; GDZ/eudml full text not retrieved). The inequality used below is GB-P Theorem 6.4, which attributes the semigroup form to [A-M] and to Kang / Russell; no step cites a page of the 1975 text that I have not seen.
./xmodel/m-inf-hostile-review-sol56-20260831.log:346:    42	- Barrolleta–García Barroso–Płoski, arXiv:1407.0176, AM semigroups and conductor `c ≤ (n-1)(n-2)`.
./xmodel/m-inf-hostile-review-sol56-20260831.log:348:    44	- García Barroso–et al., arXiv:2209.04232, conductors of AM semigroups.
