./xmodel/block-descent-a1-rank4-r1-splice-census-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:2750:+The unbounded direction is honestly named if read as "not bounded by affine delta or by the finite `S4` colouring computation." It is not an attainment theorem for every `n`. The weakest replacement is an explicit hypothesis: the projective closure at the unique infinite point has exactly the claimed two-arrowhead splice type, with the only unbounded parameter the mutual `T(2,2n)` linking core and no additional algebraic-link shapes of component genus at most two.
./xmodel/block-descent-a1-rank4-r1-splice-census-hostile-review-gpt55-20260831.log:2776:+**`T(2,2n)` core: CONFIRMED.** Two transpositions generate a subgroup of order at most `6`, never `S4`.
