./xmodel/round1033-hf-dossier-delta6-grok46-20260831.log:2:I'll verify the frozen-input hashes first, then write the report skeleton and start assembling the Heegaard-Floer dossier from those copies.Hashes match. Next I’ll write the report skeleton, then read the frozen cards and the conductor-12 census.Hashes checked out. I’ll finish the census and pull the charged one-place interface so the affine-singularity typing is taken from the frozen scope, not assumed.The census sequence looks like an infinity delta-sequence, not a sole affine semigroup. I’ll pin that interface in the frozen one-place papers and in Assi–García-Sánchez before filling any singularity records.The census sequence is an Abhyankar semigroup at infinity, not a sole affine cusp. I’ll pin the primary theorems next, then write the charge and interface sections.I have the literature pins and the candidate arithmetic. Next I’ll fill the report section by section, starting with charge, interface, and the first conductor-12 curve.The first `Delta_aff=6` candidate is **OPEN**. Report: `xmodel/round1033-hf-dossier-delta6-grok46-20260831.md`.
./xmodel/round1033-hf-dossier-delta6-grok46-20260831.log:4:**Candidate.** Census row `(6,4,9)` only (the twin `(9,6,4)` was not touched). Reduced embedding degree `d=6`, genus split `10 = 6 + 4`.
./xmodel/round1033-hf-dossier-delta6-grok46-20260831.log:6:**What is determined.** The Assi–García-Sánchez sequence is the Abhyankar semigroup at infinity, `Gamma=<6,4,9>`, conductor 12, large-sphere knot `C_(2,9)(T(2,3))`. The local germ of the projective closure at infinity is a different object: unibranch `S_infty=<2,9>`, `delta=4`, link `T(2,9)`. That local semigroup is constant on the whole reduced `(6,4,9)` family.
./xmodel/round1033-hf-dossier-delta6-grok46-20260831.log:8:**What is not determined.** The census does **not** give a sole affine cusp. `Delta_aff` is only a sum. The first AG-S associated curve `(y^3-x^2)^2-x^3`, parametrized by `( (t^3-1)^2, t^4-t )`, has one affine singularity: three smooth branches through the origin with a common tangent. That is `UNLICENSED_MULTIBRANCH`. Borodzik–Livingston 2014 and Borodzik–Hedden–Livingston 2017 need every singularity unibranch; Borodzik–Liu–Zemke 2024 Theorem 6.4 licences only `T(2,2n)` among noncuspidal points (a node is `n=1`). None of those hypotheses hold.
./xmodel/round1033-hf-dossier-delta6-grok46-20260831.log:10:**Inequality.** Not evaluated on the candidate (that would invent an affine semigroup). Controls, by exact integer arithmetic: the unicuspidal quartic `X^4+Y^3Z=0` passes Borodzik–Livingston 2014 Theorem 6.5 at `j=1` (`R(5)=3`); a hand-mutated gap set of the same size fails (`R~(5)=2`).
./xmodel/round1033-hf-dossier-delta6-grok46-20260831.log:12:**Not a kill and not a construction target.** No licensed inequality was applied, so nothing was violated; `PASS_NECESSARY_ONLY` would require a complete licensed dossier. Fable’s “JEMS 2014” citation is wrong — the paper is Forum Math. Sigma 2 (2014) e28. No `charge_basis` line: no new exit price.
