./xmodel/sol-k2c.log:2955:A decisive obstruction has emerged, but it is narrower than a residue-A counterexample: generalized Hénon automorphisms give genuine Keller pairs with fixed \(\mathrm{td}=1\) and an arbitrarily long characteristic chain whose product is exactly \(42\cdot2^r\). This proves that polynomial origin, the full homogeneous Jacobian identity, and Abhyankar–Moh semigroup compatibility do not by themselves turn bounded topological degree into a carrier bound. I’m checking the exact indexing and then will state separately that this family is not residue A, so the td\(=6\) realization remains open.
