./xmodel/websweep-20260824T1916Z-makar-shape-recovery-audit-codex.md:32:1. **Lemma on the leading monomial.**  If `p,q in C[x,y]` are algebraically independent and leading monomials are taken in `w`-lexicographic order (`x >> y`) for any fixed weight `w`, then the semigroup of leading monomials of elements of `C[p,q]` contains two algebraically independent monomials.  The proof compares the quadratic growth `dim Span{p^i q^j:i+j<=N}=binom(N+2,2)` with linear growth if all leading exponent vectors lie on one ray.
