./xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-sol56.log:5944:+For a surviving rank-four candidate, homogenize the proposed irreducible `A1`-normalized one-place curve to $\bar B\subset\mathbb{CP}^2$. When every singularity of $\bar B$ is unibranch, the candidate is a rational cuspidal plane curve; its projective degree and local value semigroups must satisfy the Heegaard–Floer correction-term inequalities of Borodzik–Livingston and their arbitrary-genus extension. These are effective inequalities on semigroup-counting functions, so the delta-sequence compiler can test them by integer arithmetic. The primary sources are Borodzik–Livingston, *Heegaard Floer homology and rational cuspidal curves*, Forum Math. Sigma 2 (2014), e28, [arXiv:1304.1062](https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.1062), and Borodzik–Hedden–Livingston, *Plane algebraic curves of arbitrary genus via Heegaard Floer homology*, Comment. Math. Helv. 92 (2017), 215–256, [doi:10.4171/CMH/411](https://doi.org/10.4171/CMH/411).
./xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-sol56.log:5948:+For noncuspidal controls, Borodzik–Liu–Zemke construct link-Floer/knotification obstructions and explicitly treat transverse double points in *Heegaard Floer homology, knotifications of links, and plane curves with noncuspidal singularities*, Algebr. Geom. Topol. 24 (2024), 4837–4889, [doi:10.2140/agt.2024.24.4837](https://doi.org/10.2140/agt.2024.24.4837). That paper licenses a node branch of the compiler and a regression against the promoted one-node kill; it does **not** by itself license arbitrary tangencies. A tangential or general multibranch record therefore returns typed `OPEN` until its exact link-cobordism hypotheses are proved.
./xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-sol56.log:5972:+Implement a small, exact `attainment_sieve` (ordinary integer arithmetic, no CAS). Its typed input is `(projective_degree, normalization_genus, singularity_records[])`; each singularity record declares `UNIBRANCH_SEMIGROUP`, `TRANSVERSE_NODE`, or `UNLICENSED_MULTIBRANCH`, and the infinity record additionally carries the reduced delta-sequence and the declared semigroup map. The program should:
./xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-sol56.log:5974:+1. verify the genus formula and semigroup conductors;
./xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-sol56.log:5975:+2. compute the infimal-convolution/semigroup-counting functions required by the cited Floer theorem;
./xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-sol56.log:5976:+3. emit the first violated inequality with all counts as a replay certificate, or `PASS_NECESSARY_ONLY`;
./xmodel/ideation-20260831T1033Z-sol56.log:5977:+4. return `OPEN` on a tangency or missing projective degree instead of guessing a semigroup.
